WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
Hello, champ! Welcome!

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:15.120
Something new: the Maths track!

3
00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:22.300
Numbers Computers Love · Chapter 1

4
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:34.550
We use 10 digits. Computers use just 2!

5
00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:42.700
Meet Meera, and her friend Kabir

6
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:54.060
Secret plan: send a number with 3 lamps

7
00:00:54.060 --> 00:01:08.450
Each lamp is only ON or OFF. How to show 5?

8
00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:18.620
Computers do this all the time!

9
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:29.820
Inside a computer: tiny on/off switches

10
00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:39.090
ON = 1 · OFF = 0

11
00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:47.520
Games, photos, songs: all 0s and 1s!

12
00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:58.510
Counting with 0 and 1 is called BINARY

13
00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:10.800
Us: 0 to 9 · Binary: just 0 and 1

14
00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:19.640
One light = one BIT (a single 0 or 1)

15
00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:26.460
Your 3 fingers = 3 light switches

16
00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:32.800
Finger up = 1 · Finger down = 0

17
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:45.010
All down = 000 · All up = 111

18
00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:51.450
Each place has its own value

19
00:02:51.450 --> 00:03:01.750
Left = 4 · Middle = 2 · Right = 1

20
00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:08.450
Add the values of the lights that are ON

21
00:03:08.450 --> 00:03:22.170
1 0 1 → 4 + 0 + 1 = 5

22
00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:29.720
Kabir reads it: five laddoos!

23
00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:38.480
0 = 000 (all off)

24
00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:48.320
1 = 001 · 2 = 010

25
00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:56.800
3 = 011 (2 + 1)

26
00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:06.690
4 = 100 · 5 = 101 (4 + 1)

27
00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:13.610
Each number adds one more laddoo

28
00:04:13.610 --> 00:04:29.870
001 and 100: the same number?

29
00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:42.060
001 = 1 · 100 = 4. The place matters!

30
00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:51.880
Like 23 and 32: same digits, not the same!

31
00:04:51.880 --> 00:05:01.450
Light game: what number is 010?

32
00:05:01.450 --> 00:05:09.440
010 → 0 + 2 + 0 = 2

33
00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:16.560
Which lights show 4?

34
00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:24.240
4 = 100 (only the left light)

35
00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:42.330
001, 010, 011, … what comes next?

36
00:05:42.330 --> 00:05:51.910
Not 012! Binary has no digit 2

37
00:05:51.910 --> 00:06:01.670
011 is 3, so next is 4 = 100

38
00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:05.550
Your turn: practice check

39
00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:19.390
Show 3 using three on/off lights

40
00:06:19.390 --> 00:06:35.320
Off, on, on → 011 → 2 + 1 = 3

41
00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:42.020
Binary uses only 0 and 1

42
00:06:42.020 --> 00:06:45.000
ON = 1 · OFF = 0

43
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:50.850
Three lights are worth 4, 2, 1

44
00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:56.960
3 = 011 · 5 = 101

45
00:06:56.960 --> 00:07:04.030
Chapter 1 done!

46
00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:10.830
Next: Quiz · Tap Finish
